To understand how the models were making their predictions, SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations) plots were used to analyze feature importance and influence. This analysis yielded several key insights that align perfectly with the “ECC's” theoretical structure:
Feature importance was not uniform but clustered into distinct "attractor corridors," indicating that the models were learning the symbolic identity classes proposed by the theory.

