Further tests on "Entropy Stratification" revealed that model performance increased significantly when trained on subsets of the data corresponding to higher entropy layers, with R² scores rising from ~0.74 in low-entropy strata to ~0.91 in high-entropy strata. This provides strong evidence that higher entropy regions support more stable and coherent symbolic projections, a central prediction of the “ECC.”
